@@ -0,0 +1,145 @@
+# Editing dependencies
+
+-----
+
+Rather than editing `pyproject.toml` by hand, you can use the `hatch dep add`
+and `hatch dep remove` commands to manage the dependencies of your project
+and its environments. Every edit preserves the existing formatting and
+comments of `pyproject.toml`, and nothing is written unless the whole set of
+requested changes is valid.
+
+## Adding dependencies
+
+By default, requirements are appended to `project.dependencies`:
+
+```console
+$ hatch dep add "requests>=2"
+```
+
+The stored text is exactly what you passed, except that markers use single
+quotes to avoid escaping inside the TOML string. If a dependency with the
+same (normalized) distribution name is already present in the target field,
+the command exits with an error; pass `--force` to replace the existing
+entry in place instead:
+
+```console
+$ hatch dep add "requests>=3" --force
+```
+
+`--force` also removes marker-split duplicates of the same name, leaving
+exactly one entry for the requested requirement.
+
+### Features
+
+Use `--optional`/`-o` to add to a feature of
+[`project.optional-dependencies`](../../config/metadata.md#optional) instead,
+creating the feature if it does not exist yet:
+
+```console
+$ hatch dep add pytest -o test
+```
+
+The option may be given multiple times to add the same requirement to
+several features atomically – if any of those features would raise a
+conflict, none of them are modified.
+
+### Dependency groups
+
+Use `--group`/`-g` to add to a [PEP 735](https://peps.python.org/pep-0735/)
+[dependency group](../../config/dependency.md), creating the group if it
+does not exist yet:
+
+```console
+$ hatch dep add ruff -g lint
+```
+
+Groups may contain [`include-group`](https://peps.python.org/pep-0735/#specifying-a-project-as-a-dependency)
+entries that reference other groups. Those entries are left untouched by
+`dep add` and `dep remove`.
+
+### Environments
+
+Use `--env` to add to the [`dependencies`](../../config/environment/overview.md#dependencies)
+of an environment defined in `tool.hatch.envs`:
+
+```console
+$ hatch dep add ipython --env default
+```
+
+The environment must already be defined, except for the `default`
+environment whose table is created on demand. Add `--extra` to target the
+environment's [`extra-dependencies`](../../config/environment/overview.md#extra-dependencies)
+instead:
+
+```console
+$ hatch dep add debugpy --env default --extra
+```
+
+The `--env` option cannot be combined with `--optional` or `--group`.
+
+Fields that are declared [dynamic](../../config/metadata.md#dynamic) cannot
+be edited and produce an error.
+
+### Dry runs
+
+Passing `--dry-run` performs the full validation cycle and prints a unified
+diff of the change that would be applied to `pyproject.toml`, without
+writing the file:
+
+```console
+$ hatch dep add "requests>=2" --dry-run
+--- a/pyproject.toml
++++ b/pyproject.toml
+@@ -1,3 +1,3 @@
+ [project]
+ name = "demo"
+-dependencies = ["click"]
++dependencies = ["click", "requests>=2"]
+```
+
+## Removing dependencies
+
+The remove command takes bare distribution names and matches entries by
+their normalized name, ignoring extras, version specifiers and markers:
+
+```console
+$ hatch dep remove requests
+```
+
+Without any scope option, every static location is searched: the project
+dependencies, all optional features and all dependency groups. Every
+matching entry (including marker-split duplicates for the same name) is
+removed, and each removal is reported. If a name is not found anywhere,
+the command exits with an error and nothing is written.
+
+Use `--optional`/`-o`, `--group`/`-g` or `--env` (optionally with
+`--extra`) to restrict the removal to specific fields:
+
+```console
+$ hatch dep remove pytest -o test
+$ hatch dep remove ruff -g lint
+$ hatch dep remove ipython --env default
+$ hatch dep remove debugpy --env default --extra
+```
+
+Environments are intentionally *not* part of the default scope – a bare
+`hatch dep remove <name>` will not touch any environment table. If you
+want to remove a dependency from an environment, pass `--env` explicitly.
+
+Requirement strings (with extras, version specifiers, markers or URLs) are
+rejected as arguments – if you tried `hatch dep remove "requests>=2"` you
+will get an error hinting that only the bare name should be passed.
+
+`--dry-run` behaves the same as it does for `dep add`.
+
+## Atomicity
+
+Both commands validate every requested change before writing anything.
+When you ask to add or remove multiple dependencies across multiple
+targets, either the whole change lands or none of it does. If a single
+one of the changes is invalid, the command exits with a non-zero status
+and `pyproject.toml` is not touched.
+
+The write itself goes through an atomic ``os.replace`` on the same
+directory, so a crash midway through leaves you with the *previous*
+`pyproject.toml` bytes rather than a half-written file.
