+    always a typo. When no scope option is given, the default scope is
+    everything the project statically declares – project dependencies,
+    every optional feature and every dependency group. Environments are
+    intentionally *excluded* from that default: an env-only dependency is
+    a much more surgical thing to remove and we don't want a blanket
